# act — https://github.com/nektos/act. Ported from resume-2026 (M0.23).
#
# catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest is the closest public match to GitHub's
# hosted Ubuntu runner and ships multi-arch (amd64 + arm64), so it also runs
# unmodified on Apple Silicon. The label on the left is the one every
# workflow pins in `runs-on:` (ubuntu-26.04 since MB.37, not the floating
# ubuntu-latest) — bump both together or act finds no platform for the jobs.
# --pull=false leaves the first-use pull to docker and skips a redundant
# registry round-trip on every later run.
-P ubuntu-26.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--pull=false
